E["npc:maurin-bonesplitter"] = {t="npc",n="Maurin Bonesplitter",z="desolace",s="Maurin Bonesplitter is a Forsaken scholar and spellcaster stationed at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace. Appointed by Keldran to monitor demonic cult activity, he leverages his deep understanding of ancient lore to dismantle the Burning Blade. Maurin regards the cultists with sheer contempt, viewing them as fools blind to the dark entities pulling their strings.",h="Maurin Bonesplitter is a Forsaken scholar and spellcaster stationed at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace.",sec={{t="A Scholar Among Outcasts",b="While Ghost Walker Post primarily serves as a tauren and Horde outpost amidst the arid wastes of Desolace, Maurin Bonesplitter stands apart as one of its few undead occupants. Rather than a brutish soldier, Maurin is a learned spellcaster possessing extensive knowledge of forbidden histories and occult forces. His arcane aptitude and sharp intellect caught the eye of Keldran, who dispatched him to the region to observe the growing demonic presence and coordinate targeted strikes against it.",sp=0},{t="Contempt for the Burning Blade",b="Maurin directs most of his malice toward the Burning Blade cult entrenched across Desolace. He harbors utter disgust for their reckless ambition, mocking the cultists for failing to understand that their borrowed power merely binds them as thralls to their demonic masters. Through concoctions and ritual knowledge, Maurin enlists Horde adventurers to systematically disrupt the cult's summonings and undermine their operations across the barren landscape.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Maurin Bonesplitter?",a="Maurin Bonesplitter is a Forsaken mage and scholar residing at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace. Appointed by Keldran, he uses his knowledge of ancient lore and dark magic to root out the Burning Blade cult operating in the region.",al={"maurin bonesplitter lore","who is maurin","maurin desolace"}},{q="Why is an undead staying at a tauren post?",a="Ghost Walker Post acts as a key Horde settlement in Desolace. Maurin was stationed there by Keldran specifically because the outpost provides an ideal staging ground to observe and combat the Burning Blade cultists infesting the surrounding wilderness.",al={"why is maurin at ghost walker post","undead in desolace"}},{q="What is Maurin's opinion of the Burning Blade?",a="Maurin views the Burning Blade with deep contempt. He sees them as pathetic, ignorant pawns who delusionally believe they wield true power, entirely oblivious to the reality that they are merely puppets of demonic masters.",al={"maurin burning blade","why does maurin hate burning blade"}},{q="Who sent Maurin Bonesplitter to Desolace?",a="Maurin was appointed to his role in Desolace by Keldran. Recognizing Maurin's extensive knowledge of cult practices and ancient lore, Keldran tasked him with actively hindering and eventually eliminating the Burning Blade from the zone.",al={"who sent maurin","maurin keldran","maurin boss"}},{q="What kind of tasks does Maurin give adventurers?",a="Maurin employs adventurers to disrupt Burning Blade operations, investigate corruption, and deliver specially crafted concoctions and devices to sever the cult's hold over local spirits and demonic entities.",al={"maurin quests","what does maurin want"}},{q="Is Maurin affiliated with the Cenarion Circle or the Horde?",a="Maurin is a loyal member of the Forsaken and serves the Horde. He operates strictly from the Horde encampment at Ghost Walker Post, aiding Horde champions in cleansing the wastes of cultist activity.",al={"is maurin horde","maurin faction"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Maurin demonstrates that Forsaken strength relies as much on cunning arcane research and exploiting enemy weaknesses as it does on sheer necromantic might.",["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks will recognize Maurin's acute understanding of demonic pacts, though his disdain serves as a sharp reminder of the peril that comes with serving greater fiends.",["class:Mage"]="Mages visiting Ghost Walker Post can appreciate Maurin's calculated, intellectual approach to unraveling dark rituals with specialized counters.",["faction:Horde"]="Maurin represents Undercity's specialized support to the Horde's western outposts, bringing dark academic knowledge to assist tauren allies against demonic corruption."},kw={"burning blade","concoction","corrupter","desolace","forsaken","ghost walker post","keldran","maurin bonesplitter"},rel={"subzone:ghost-walker-post","zone:desolace","npc:keldran","topic:forsaken","quest:1431"},src={"Maurin Bonesplitter"}}
E["npc:misha"] = {t="npc",n="Misha",z="desolace",s="Misha is the loyal bear companion of Rexxar, the Champion of the Horde. Rescued as an orphaned cub, she wanders Kalimdor faithfully at the Mok'nathal beastmaster's side.",h="Misha is the loyal bear companion of Rexxar, the Champion of the Horde.",sec={{t="A Boundless Bond",b="Rexxar discovered Misha as an orphaned cub beside her slain mother in the Ruins of Ravenwind in Feralas. Recognizing a kindred solitary spirit, the wandering Mok'nathal adopted her and gave her a name. Together they ventured north into the arid wilds of Desolace, forging a fierce, protective partnership that has weathered countless wildernesses and bloody battles.",sp=0},{t="Defender of Durotar",b="Misha is far more than a tame pet; she is a seasoned warrior. She fought alongside Rexxar in the brutal conflict against Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore at Theramore Isle, helping ensure the young Horde's survival. When not in battle, her keen senses and strength serve as an extension of Rexxar's will, even carrying fallen allies such as the orc Byrok back to Orgrimmar.",sp=0},{t="Wilds of Kalimdor",b="Currently, travelers venturing along the long tracks through the Stonetalon Mountains, Desolace, and Feralas can spot Misha padding quietly beside Rexxar. Though fierce enough to tear apart any predator foolish enough to threaten them, she remains Rexxar's steadfast anchor in an otherwise untrustworthy world.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Misha?",a="Misha is a ferocious brown bear and the lifelong companion of Rexxar, the Champion of the Horde. She wanders the wilds alongside him across central Kalimdor.",al={"rexxars bear","who is the bear with rexxar","misha bear"}},{q="Where did Rexxar find Misha?",a="Rexxar found Misha as a small cub in the Ruins of Ravenwind in Feralas, stranded beside her dead mother. Seeing that they were both alone in the wild, Rexxar took her in.",al={"where did rexxar get misha","misha backstory","how did rexxar meet misha"}},{q="Where can Misha be found right now?",a="Misha roams along the long patrol paths of the Stonetalon Mountains, Desolace, and Feralas, faithfully walking alongside Rexxar on his endless wanderings.",al={"misha location","where is misha","find misha"}},{q="Did Misha take part in the founding of Durotar?",a="Yes. Following the Third War, Misha accompanied Rexxar into battle against Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's forces at Theramore Isle to defend the fledgling Horde.",al={"misha theramore","did misha fight daelin","misha third war"}},{q="Is Misha hostile to Alliance players?",a="Yes. As the companion of the Champion of the Horde, Misha will fiercely defend Rexxar and attack any Alliance trespassers who draw too close.",al={"can alliance attack misha","is misha aggressive"}},{q="Why does Rexxar prefer beasts like Misha to people?",a="Disillusioned by the deceit and warfare of humanoid races, Rexxar chose the solitude of the wilderness. He believes beasts are direct and honest, finding in Misha a companion devoid of betrayal.",al={"why does rexxar keep beasts","rexxar bear companion"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="For hunters, Misha represents the ultimate ideal of an animal companion: an unbreakable lifelong partnership forged through mutual respect rather than mere dominance.",["faction:Horde"]="Misha fought alongside Rexxar to secure the fledgling Horde's freedom at Theramore Isle, earning the quiet respect of veterans across Durotar."},kw={"bear","beastmaster","desolace","feralas","misha","ravenwind","rexxar","stonetalon"},rel={"zone:desolace","zone:feralas","zone:stonetalon","subzone:ruins-of-ravenwind","subzone:theramore-isle","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde","topic:third-war"},src={"Misha"}}
E["npc:taiga-wisemane"] = {t="npc",n="Taiga Wisemane",z="desolace",s="Taiga Wisemane is a tauren elder residing in Shadowprey Village along the rugged western coast of Desolace. Watchful of demonic meddling across the barren wastes, he works to thwart the Burning Blade cult entrenched in the region. He directs Horde champions to disrupt demonic rituals and seal open gateways before the Burning Legion gains ground.",h="Taiga Wisemane is a tauren elder residing in Shadowprey Village along the rugged western coast of Desolace.",sec={{t="A Watchful Eye in Shadowprey",b="Though Shadowprey Village is predominantly a Darkspear troll fishing settlement tucked away against the ocean, Taiga Wisemane has taken up station there to monitor the dark sorceries stirring across Desolace. He remains acutely aware of the spiritual corruption bleeding into the soil, keeping his focus fixed eastward where shadow cults and demonic remnants fester among ancient ruins.",sp=0},{t="Stemming the Demonic Tide",b="The Burning Blade cult operates actively out of Thunder Axe Fortress, experimenting with dark artifacts to widen their influence. Recognizing the peril this poses to all inhabitants of Desolace, Taiga tasks capable adventurers with infiltrating the fortress to claim the Demon Box—an occult chest holding the Hand of Iruxos. Through this severing blow, he aims to rob the cult of the primary focus they rely upon to tear the veil between worlds.",sp=1},{t="Sealing the Coven's Portals",b="Securing the Hand of Iruxos is only the first step of Taiga's plan. At Mannoroc Coven to the south, the Burning Blade has already torn open active demonic rifts. By turning the dark focus against its creators, Taiga directs trusted champions to channel the artifact's energy directly into the gateways, closing the conduits before the Burning Legion can pour reinforcements into the heart of Kalimdor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Taiga Wisemane?",a="Taiga Wisemane is a tauren elder staying in Shadowprey Village on the western coast of Desolace. He acts as an advisor and quest giver dedicated to tracking and countering demonic rituals enacted by the Burning Blade cult throughout the region.",al={"who is taiga","taiga wisemane lore","taiga shadowprey"}},{q="Why is a tauren living in Shadowprey Village?",a="While Shadowprey is primarily a troll settlement, it is the Horde's main outpost along the Desolace coast. Taiga stays there to keep watch over the desolate wastes and enlist passing Horde travelers to neutralize nearby demonic threats.",al={"why is taiga in shadowprey","taiga troll village","tauren in troll town"}},{q="What is the Burning Blade doing in Desolace?",a="Operating from Thunder Axe Fortress and Mannoroc Coven, the Burning Blade cult is opening demonic gateways to summon forces of the Burning Legion into Kalimdor. Taiga works to undo their efforts before the wasteland is completely overrun.",al={"burning blade desolace","what are the cultists doing","thunder axe fortress cultists"}},{q="What is the Hand of Iruxos?",a="The Hand of Iruxos is a demonic artifact locked within a Demon Box at Thunder Axe Fortress. The Burning Blade means to use its foul energies to pry open portals to the Nether, but Taiga devises a way to turn the hand's magic against the rifts to seal them shut.",al={"hand of iruxos","what is demon box","demon box relic"}},{q="What happens at Mannoroc Coven?",a="Mannoroc Coven is an unholy site in southern Desolace where the Burning Blade successfully established demonic portals. Under Taiga Wisemane's instruction, adventurers take the Hand of Iruxos to the site to forcefully shut down the gateways.",al={"mannoroc coven portals","what is mannoroc coven","desolace portals"}},{q="Does Taiga belong to a specific tauren tribe?",a="Taiga carries the Wisemane surname, reflecting his role as an elder deeply concerned with spiritual balance and demonic corruption, though he serves the wider Horde gathered under the banner of the united tribes.",al={"taiga tribe","wisemane tribe","is taiga bloodhoof"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Taiga provides crucial direction for Horde champions traveling through Desolace, ensuring that the outpost of Shadowprey Village remains shielded from demonic encroachment.",["race:Tauren"]="For tauren travelers, Taiga represents the duty to heal and protect Kalimdor from unnatural demonic blight, standing against the dark legacy that has scarred Desolace.",["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks will find Taiga's understanding of the Hand of Iruxos notable, as he uses the dark relic's own resonance to collapse demonic portals rather than banish them through holy rites."},kw={"burning blade","demon box","desolace","hand of iruxos","mannoroc coven","shadowprey village","taiga wisemane","thunder axe fortress"},rel={"subzone:shadowprey-village","zone:desolace","subzone:thunder-axe-fortress","subzone:mannoroc-coven","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Taiga Wisemane"}}
E["subzone:bolgan-s-hole"] = {t="subzone",n="Bolgan's Hole",z="desolace",s="Bolgan's Hole is a subterranean cavern nestled in the southern cliffs of Gelkis Village in Desolace. It serves as the inner sanctum of the Gelkis centaur clan, housing their highest chieftains and sacred earth relics.",h="Bolgan's Hole is a subterranean cavern nestled in the southern cliffs of Gelkis Village in Desolace.",sec={{t="The Gelkis Seat of Power",b="Carved deep into the craggy bluffs overlooking the Gelkis encampment, Bolgan's Hole functions as the command center for the tribe. It is here that the ruling khan holds court, surrounded by veteran guards and the tribe's most influential shamans. The cavern offers natural fortification against rival clans, most notably the bloodthirsty Magram centaur to the east.",sp=0},{t="Tears of the Earth Princess",b="Beyond its military importance, the cave possesses profound religious significance to the Gelkis. Luminous blue mineral formations known as the tears of Theradras sprout from the damp stone walls. Gelkis shamans obsessively harvest and guard these crystals, revering them as divine blessings that confer the subterranean protection of Princess Theradras, the primal earth elemental mother of the centaur race.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Bolgan's Hole located?",a="Bolgan's Hole is a cave situated in the southern part of Gelkis Village, tucked into the hills of southern Desolace.",al={"bolgans hole location","where is bolgan's hole","bolgan cave entrance"}},{q="Who lives inside Bolgan's Hole?",a="The cave houses the high leadership of the Gelkis centaur, including their clan khan—such as Khan Shaka—as well as their inner circle of protectors and mystical shamans.",al={"who is in bolgan's hole","bolgans hole boss","gelkis khan location"}},{q="What are the glowing blue crystals inside the cave?",a="The crystals are known as the tears of Theradras. The Gelkis revere them as physical manifestations of their earth mother's favor, believing the stones grant mystical protection to those who possess them.",al={"blue crystals in bolgan's hole","tears of theradras","bolgan's hole rocks"}},{q="Can players enter Bolgan's Hole safely?",a="By default, the Gelkis centaur inside are aggressively hostile to outsiders. However, travelers who align themselves with the Gelkis by slaughtering their hated rivals, the Magram clan, can earn standing to walk the cave in peace.",al={"is bolgan's hole hostile","friendly to gelkis","can i go inside bolgans hole"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The cavern offers a grim demonstration of how earth worship can be corrupted when tied to the violent legacy of Princess Theradras rather than the natural balance of the spirits."},kw={"bolgan's hole","centaur","desolace","gelkis","khan shaka","khan shodo","tears of theradras"},rel={"subzone:gelkis-village","topic:centaur","zone:desolace"},src={"Bolgan's Hole"}}
E["subzone:ethel-rethor"] = {t="subzone",n="Ethel Rethor",z="desolace",s="Ethel Rethor is an ancient night elven ruin situated along the rugged northwestern coast of Desolace. While a solitary, sealed tower still rises above the waves, the majority of the sunken settlement now lies submerged in the sea and overrun by hostile naga.",h="Ethel Rethor is an ancient night elven ruin situated along the rugged northwestern coast of Desolace.",sec={{t="A Drowned Relic",b="Perched on the desolate coast of western Kalimdor, Ethel Rethor stands as a haunting reminder of the ancient night elven civilization that flourished before the Great Sundering. Much of the grand architecture has collapsed into the ocean depths, leaving only shattered foundations and a lone, weathered tower protruding from the surf. A small bridge extends toward the tower's sealed portal, but the structure remains shut tight against the elements and intruders alike. The submerged chambers and surrounding shallows have become a stronghold for coastal naga, making the waters treacherous for any who wander near.",sp=0},{t="Watchers on the Shore",b="Despite its remote location and serpentine infestation, Ethel Rethor draws travelers interested in Kalimdor's forgotten histories and ongoing threats. An agent of the Argent Dawn, Azore Aldamort, maintains a watchful presence near the ruins, monitoring the naga menace and offering aid to intrepid adventurers willing to dive into the sunken passages. Between the aquatic dangers offshore and the barren wastes inland, the ruins serve as a lonely coastal crossroads.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Ethel Rethor?",a="Ethel Rethor is a ruined night elven coastal settlement in northwestern Desolace. Most of its former structures are now submerged beneath the sea, leaving behind a solitary offshore tower and drowned stonework.",al={"ethel rethor lore","what is this place desolace","ethel rethor ruin"}},{q="Who controls Ethel Rethor now?",a="The sunken ruins and adjacent reefs are occupied by naga. Like many ancient Kaldorei sites along the coast, the serpentine creatures have laid claim to the drowned halls and patrol the surrounding shallows aggressively.",al={"who lives in ethel rethor","ethel rethor monsters","naga at ethel rethor"}},{q="Can you go inside the tower?",a="The tower rising from the sea features a small bridge leading to an entrance, but the doorway remains firmly sealed shut. Travelers can only explore its exterior and dive into the sunken ruins beneath it.",al={"open ethel rethor tower","ethel rethor door","inside ethel rethor"}},{q="Why is the Argent Dawn here?",a="An Argent Dawn representative, Azore Aldamort, is stationed near the ruins. While the Dawn primarily focuses on the Scourge in the east, their operatives across Kalimdor monitor unusual magical disturbances, ancient ruins, and emerging threats like the naga.",al={"argent dawn in desolace","azore aldamor ethel rethor","argent dawn npc desolace"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Ethel Rethor is a somber monument to their lost empire, reminding them of the cataclysmic Sundering and the mutated brethren who now prowl the sunken halls.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance travelers moving through the hostile barrens of Desolace can find a rare neutral friendly face stationed near the ruins in the Argent Dawn observer Azore Aldamort."},kw={"argent dawn","azore aldamor","desolace","desolace coast","ethel rethor","kaldorei ruins","naga","sunken ruins"},rel={"zone:desolace","topic:naga","topic:argent-dawn","subzone:shadowprey-village"},src={"Ethel Rethor"}}
E["subzone:foulspore-pools"] = {t="subzone",n="Foulspore Pools",z="desolace",s="The Foulspore Pools are a subterranean cavern system beneath Desolace that serves as the orange-crystal approach to Maraudon. Bathed in unnatural fungal warmth, the cavern is filled with polluted pools, basilisks, and aggressive earth elementals. It is also the sanctuary of the dryad Cavindra, who watches over one of the few clean springs remaining in the depths.",h="The Foulspore Pools are a subterranean cavern system beneath Desolace that serves as the orange-crystal...",sec={{t="The Orange Tunnels",b="Reached through the southern passage out of Zaetar's Choice, the Foulspore Pools form a humid, eerie threshold to Maraudon. Glittering orange crystals hang from the stone overhead, dripping foul moisture into stagnant ponds that bubble across the cavern floor. Hostile subterranean basilisks and corrupted earth elementals stalk the shores of these tainted waters. Deeper in the hollow lies the instance portal leading into Maraudon's Foulspore Caverns, flanked by the grim reminder of Princess Theradras's festering influence on the earth.",sp=0},{t="Cavindra's Respite",b="Amid the oppressive rot and sulfurous orange glow, a solitary dryad named Cavindra maintains a delicate sanctuary. Resting beside a tiny pool of untainted water, she aids travelers willing to delve into the tomb-city beyond. Her presence stands in stark contrast to the surrounding decay, embodying the Cenarion circle's desperate hope to heal the tragedy wrought by Zaetar and Theradras.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do I get to the Foulspore Pools?",a="Head down into the cavern complex beneath Desolace to the crossroads known as Zaetar's Choice. From there, take the southern tunnel glowing with orange crystals, which leads straight into the Foulspore Pools.",al={"where are foulspore pools","how to reach foulspore pools","foulspore pools entrance"}},{q="Who is Cavindra?",a="Cavindra is a dryad found beside an unpolluted pool within the caverns. As a child of the Cenarion bloodline, she keeps vigil near Maraudon's entrance and offers guidance and quests to adventurers seeking to cleanse the corruption within.",al={"dryad in maraudon","cavindra","orange side dryad"}},{q="Where does the portal at the end lead?",a="The dungeon portal at the far end of the cavern leads into the orange wing of Maraudon, specifically the Foulspore Cavern. It brings adventurers directly into the territory overrun by fungal horrors, oozes, and the Corruptor Noxxion.",al={"foulspore portal","orange instance portal maraudon"}},{q="Why are the waters orange and polluted?",a="The glowing orange crystals and tainted waters are the result of the elemental and fungal corruption spreading outward from Princess Theradras's deep lair within Maraudon, blighting the earth and twisting subterranean wildlife.",al={"why is water orange","foulspore water corruption"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The foul waters and twisted elementals here represent the tragic fallout of Zaetar's union with Theradras, making this cavern a place of mourning and duty for Cenarion druids."},kw={"basilisks","cavindra","desolace","foulspore pools","maraudon","orange crystals","zaetar's choice"},rel={"zone:desolace","subzone:zaetar-s-choice"},src={"Foulspore Pools"}}
E["subzone:gelkis-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Gelkis Village",z="desolace",s="Gelkis Village is the primary stronghold of the earth-aligned Gelkis centaur clan in southwestern Desolace. Built around a rugged ravine connected by wooden spans and cliffside paths, the settlement guards the southern route toward Feralas. Its vantage directly overlooks the main north-south road, making it a perilous crossing for any traveler who has not earned the clan's favor.",h="Gelkis Village is the primary stronghold of the earth-aligned Gelkis centaur clan in southwestern Desolace.",sec={{t="A Fortress in the Ravine",b="Gelkis Village sits in a deep, craggy gorge framed by precarious bluffs and rope bridges. Unlike the nomadic raiders of the Barrens, the Gelkis have fortified their ancestral grounds into a permanent settlement, complete with outposts spreading toward the border of Feralas. The heart of the clan's leadership lies within Bolgan's Hole, a cavern carved into the southern cliff face where Khan Shaka oversees his warriors. Travelers trekking south through Desolace must either cut a bloody path through the gorge or tread carefully, as the Gelkis view uninvited wanderers as fair game in their eternal war against their rival centaur brethren.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in Gelkis Village?",a="The settlement belongs to the Gelkis clan, one of the five warring centaur tribes native to Desolace. They are staunch earth-worshipers ruled by Khan Shaka, who resides deep in the cliffside cave known as Bolgan's Hole.",al={"gelkis residents","who controls gelkis village","centaur village south"}},{q="Why are the Gelkis centaur hostile to outsiders?",a="Centaur culture is intensely territorial and aggressive toward outsiders. However, the Gelkis hate their rival clan, the Magram, above all else. Adventurers who actively hunt Magram warriors can eventually earn the Gelkis clan's trust and enter the village safely.",al={"why are gelkis attacking","gelkis hostile","can i be friendly with gelkis"}},{q="Where is Gelkis Village located?",a="It is located in southwestern Desolace, just east and slightly south of the troll settlement of Shadowprey Village. Its ravines border the southern mountain face and overlook the trail heading directly south into Feralas.",al={"gelkis location","how to find gelkis village","where is gelkis"}},{q="What is Bolgan's Hole?",a="Bolgan's Hole is a large cavern carved into the southern rock wall of the ravine, connected to the rest of the village via elevated bridges and bluffs. It serves as the inner sanctuary and seat of power for the Gelkis Khan.",al={"bolgans hole","cave in gelkis village","where is gelkis khan"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Centaur drove the tauren from their ancestral lands for generations; seeing the Gelkis fortified in their rocky bastions is a bitter reminder of their enduring threat to Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="With the Darkspear settlement of Shadowprey Village resting directly to the west on the coast, the fortified presence of the Gelkis poses an ongoing threat to nearby Horde operations."},kw={"bolgan's hole","centaur","desolace","feralas","gelkis","khan shaka","magram","shadowprey"},rel={"subzone:bolgan-s-hole","zone:desolace","topic:centaur","subzone:shadowprey-village","zone:feralas"},src={"Gelkis Village"}}
E["subzone:ghost-walker-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Ghost Walker Post",z="desolace",s="Ghost Walker Post is a modest tauren settlement situated in the heart of Desolace right beside the ancient Kodo Graveyard. Far more exposed to regional dangers than Shadowprey Village on the western coast, it serves as a frontline Horde staging ground against centaur clans and the Burning Blade.",h="Ghost Walker Post is a modest tauren settlement situated in the heart of Desolace right beside the ancient...",sec={{t="A Watch on the Wastes",b="Perched on the dusty flats of central Desolace, Ghost Walker Post provides the Horde with an austere foothold in a hostile territory. Unlike the sheltered coastal fishing haven of Shadowprey Village, this post directly faces roaming centaur marauders and demon-worshiping cultists of the Burning Blade. Facilities are spartan, offering only the bare essentials for travelers, with no inn or flight master in sight. Despite the harsh conditions, a garrison of tauren and an orcish detachment sent by Warchief Thrall keep vigilant watch over the badlands.",sp=0},{t="Guardians of the Graveyard",b="Led by the tauren shaman Gurda Wildmane, the spiritual heart of the outpost is closely entwined with the neighboring Kodo Graveyard. Shamans stationed here tend to the dying beasts that wander in to perish, helping ease them into the next life and communing with their lingering spirits. Between spiritual communion and constant military readiness, the defenders of the post honor the ancient bond between the tauren and the mighty kodo amid the ashes of Desolace.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Ghost Walker Post?",a="It is a small, rugged Horde outpost located in central Desolace, established primarily by tauren with support from an orcish garrison.",al={"ghost walker post info","what is this camp","horde camp desolace"}},{q="Who leads Ghost Walker Post?",a="The post is led by Gurda Wildmane, a tauren shaman who tends to the camp's defenses and the neighboring Kodo Graveyard.",al={"who is in charge","ghost walker leader","gurda wildmane"}},{q="Why is the post located near the Kodo Graveyard?",a="Gurda Wildmane and fellow tauren shamans reside here to help ease dying kodo into their next lives and to commune with the spirits of the fallen beasts.",al={"why by kodo graveyard","kodo spirits camp","shaman kodo graveyard"}},{q="What enemies does Ghost Walker Post fight?",a="The garrison wages constant war against the local hostile centaur tribes and the sinister forces of the Burning Blade operating across Desolace.",al={"ghost walker enemies","who attacks ghost walker post","post threats"}},{q="Can I get a flight path or rest at an inn here?",a="No. The outpost provides only the bare necessities for adventurers and lacks both an innkeeper and a wind rider master. Travelers must seek transport elsewhere, such as Shadowprey Village.",al={"flight master ghost walker","innkeeper ghost walker","fp here?"}},{q="How does it compare to Shadowprey Village?",a="While Shadowprey Village is a protected troll enclave on the western coast, Ghost Walker Post is inland, heavily exposed to surrounding threats, and focused on frontier defense and spiritual duties.",al={"shadowprey vs ghost walker","other horde camp desolace"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The camp reflects the tauren's deep sacred duty to the natural world, standing as guardians beside the ancestral resting grounds of the kodo.",["class:Shaman"]="Under Gurda Wildmane, the shamans here perform the sacred work of speaking with ancient spirits and easing dying beasts into the spirit world."},kw={"burning blade","centaur","desolace","ghost walker post","gurda wildmane","horde","kodo graveyard","shadowprey village","tauren","thrall"},rel={"zone:desolace","subzone:kodo-graveyard","subzone:shadowprey-village","topic:tauren","topic:horde","topic:centaur","npc:thrall","quest:4767"},src={"Ghost Walker Post"}}
E["subzone:kodo-graveyard"] = {t="subzone",n="Kodo Graveyard",z="desolace",s="The Kodo Graveyard is a sprawling expanse in central Desolace littered with the massive, bleached remains of ancient beasts. By instinct or tradition, aging and dying kodos make a final pilgrimage to this desolate hollow to collapse among the ribs of their ancestors.",h="The Kodo Graveyard is a sprawling expanse in central Desolace littered with the massive, bleached remains of...",sec={{t="Resting Place of Titans",b="Sprawling across the grey earth of Desolace, the Kodo Graveyard holds the colossal skeletons of ancient beasts, some far larger than any living kodo seen today. Guided by an innate instinct echoing the ancient elephant legends of other worlds, dying kodos wander here to spend their final breaths among centuries of accumulated remains. This sacred peace is fragile: scavengers prowl the perimeter, and those who disturb the calcified ribs and skulls risk stirring furious kodo spirits from the dust.",sp=0},{t="A Land of Spirits",b="The boundary between the living and the dead wears exceptionally thin across the bone fields. Travelers who peer into the spirit realm find restless, towering kodo apparitions wandering silently among the dust storms. Nearby, the Horde maintains Ghost Walker Post, watching over the sacred grounds and keeping a wary eye on the wandering herds and spectral manifestations that linger around the bones.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do the kodos come here to die?",a="It is an instinctive ritual. When kodos grow ancient, sick, or near death, an innate compulsion drives them across the waste to lie down among the skeletons of their ancestors in this specific corner of Desolace.",al={"why are there bones here","kodo dying grounds","why do kodos gather here"}},{q="Why are some of the skeletons so enormous?",a="The ground contains fossils and bones dating back generations. Many of the preserved skeletons belong to ancient kodo ancestors that grew to far greater sizes than the beasts currently roaming Kalimdor.",al={"giant kodo bones","huge kodo ribs","massive bones desolace"}},{q="What happens if someone disturbs the bones?",a="Disturbing the remains often provokes the spirits of the dead. Vengeful kodo apparitions readily materialize to attack anyone attempting to scavenge or desecrate the resting place.",al={"looting kodo bones","kodo ghosts","bone collector quest"}},{q="What is Ghost Walker Post?",a="Ghost Walker Post is a small Horde encampment stationed right by the bone fields, allowing Horde travelers to rest, watch over the region's spiritual activity, and guide wanderers through central Desolace.",al={"horde camp near bones","ghost walker camp"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The kodo is a revered partner and spiritual companion to the tauren, making the desecration of these ancestral resting grounds a grave matter.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The decaying remains and spiritual resonance of the graveyard make the area around the large skeletons fertile ground for gathering Grave Moss."},kw={"desolace","ghost walker post","grave moss","kodo bones","kodo graveyard","kodo spirits"},rel={"zone:desolace","subzone:ghost-walker-post","topic:horde","subzone:vice"},src={"Kodo Graveyard"}}
E["subzone:kormek-s-hut"] = {t="subzone",n="Kormek's Hut",z="desolace",s="Kormek's Hut is a remote, ramshackle dwelling sitting amid the barren flats of north-central Desolace. Despite its desolate surroundings and mysterious namesake, it currently shelters an eccentric pair: an oddly peaceful cultist and a goblin obsessed with harvesting kodo bones.",h="Kormek's Hut is a remote, ramshackle dwelling sitting amid the barren flats of north-central Desolace.",sec={{t="A Strange Oasis of Oddities",b="Perched out in the arid wastes of north-central Desolace, this small hovel is named after a figure whose whereabouts and identity remain completely unknown. Instead of Kormek, travelers stumbling upon the hut encounter an unusual pairing living out in the middle of nowhere: Willow and Bibbly F'utzbuckle. Inside the hut sits Willow, a member of the otherwise hostile and nihilistic Twilight's Hammer who curiously treats outsiders with calm hospitality. Outside, a pen littered with sun-bleached kodo bones serves as the personal dance floor and staging ground for Bibbly, an excitable goblin captivated by the commercial potential of bone scavenging.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kormek?",a="No one knows. The hut bears Kormek's name, but neither the goblin outside nor the cultist inside explains who Kormek was, and the namesake is nowhere to be found in the wastes.",al={"who is kormek","kormek identity","where is kormek"}},{q="Why is there a friendly Twilight's Hammer cultist here?",a="Willow resides inside the hut and belongs to the Twilight's Hammer, a cult typically hostile to all mortal life. For reasons of her own, she remains non-aggressive toward travelers who drop by the remote shelter.",al={"willow twilights hammer","why is willow friendly","willow hut"}},{q="What is the goblin outside doing?",a="Bibbly F'utzbuckle spends his days excitedly dancing around an enclosure filled with kodo bones. Like many enterprising goblins, he is thrilled by the prospect of turning ancient desert remains into pure profit.",al={"bibbly futzbuckle","goblin dancing desolace","why is the goblin dancing"}},{q="Where is Kormek's Hut located?",a="The hut lies in north-central Desolace, situated in the dry, windswept flats north of the central crossroads and cemetery grounds.",al={"kormek hut location","where is kormek hut","kormek desolace"}}},kw={"bibbly f'utzbuckle","desolace","kodo bones","kormek","kormek's hut","twilight's hammer","willow"},rel={"zone:desolace","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},src={"Kormek's Hut"}}
E["subzone:magram-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Magram Village",z="desolace",s="Magram Village is the settlement of the Magram centaur clan, situated among foul yellow pools in southeastern Desolace. It serves as the primary base for the Magram as they wage relentless war against their hated rivals, the Gelkis.",h="Magram Village is the settlement of the Magram centaur clan, situated among foul yellow pools in southeastern...",sec={{t="A Stronghold in the Mire",b="Sprawled across islands and shores around stagnant, sulfurous pools in southeast Desolace, Magram Village is a rugged settlement cobbled together with crude wooden bridges and hide tents. The Magram centaur dwell here in constant vigilance against neighboring clans. Known for their sheer brutality and deep-seated animosity toward the southern Gelkis clan, the Magram are willing to tolerate outsiders only if those travelers prove their worth by slaughtering their Gelkis enemies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in Magram Village?",a="The village is home to the Magram clan, one of several warring centaur tribes native to Desolace. They live under crude hide canopies on islands connected by rough footbridges.",al={"who is here","magram residents","centaur village"}},{q="Can I enter Magram Village without being attacked?",a="Initially, the Magram centaur are hostile to all outsiders. However, travelers can earn their trust by hunting down and killing their sworn enemies, the Gelkis centaur, to raise standing with the clan.",al={"are magram friendly","magram hostile","how to visit magram village"}},{q="Why are the pools around the village yellow?",a="The pools in and around the village are tainted with sulfur and mineral runoff typical of the barren wastes of Desolace, leaving them stagnant, discolored, and polluted.",al={"yellow water","polluted pools","magram water"}},{q="Why are the Magram fighting the Gelkis?",a="The centaur clans of Desolace share a legendary, bloodthirsty rivalry. The Magram and Gelkis clans in particular have waged a bitter war for dominance over the southern reaches of the wasteland for generations.",al={"magram vs gelkis","centaur blood feud","centaur war"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Centaur savagery has plagued the tribes of Kalimdor for generations, making any settlement of these nomadic marauders an unsettling reminder of past bloodshed."},kw={"centaur","desolace","gelkis","magram","magram village","pools"},rel={"topic:centaur","zone:desolace"},src={"Magram Village"}}
E["subzone:mannoroc-coven"] = {t="subzone",n="Mannoroc Coven",z="desolace",s="Mannoroc Coven is a demon-infested ruin in southern Desolace, named after the pit lord Mannoroth. Settled among ancient night elf architecture, it stands as the largest stronghold of the Burning Legion in central Kalimdor. Cultists of the Burning Blade maintain active summoning portals here, filling the ash-choked land with felhounds, succubi, and infernals.",h="Mannoroc Coven is a demon-infested ruin in southern Desolace, named after the pit lord Mannoroth.",sec={{t="A Bastion of Fel Fire",b="Situated south of Ghost Walker Post and east of Shadowprey Village, Mannoroc Coven blankets the ancient night elf ruins in an oppressive, fel-tainted pall. The coven is commanded on the ground by Lord Azrethoc, alongside the Burning Blade warlock Jugkar Grim'rod. Together, they harness active summoning portals to pull demonic reinforcements straight into Kalimdor, including doomguards, infernals, and felhounds. Even as Horde-aligned travelers attempt to sever these links using relics like the Hand of Iruxos, new rifts continue to tear open through the scarred earth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this place called Mannoroc Coven?",a="The encampment takes its name in homage to Mannoroth the Destructor, the infamous pit lord who subjugated the orcs through the blood curse and perished in Ashenvale.",al={"who is mannoroc","mannoroc name origin","why named mannoroc"}},{q="Who rules over the coven?",a="Demonic forces here are led by the demon Lord Azrethoc. Mortal interests are directed by Jugkar Grim'rod, a warlock representing the Burning Blade cult.",al={"who leads mannoroc coven","mannoroc coven boss","azrethoc"}},{q="What ruins was the coven built upon?",a="The demonic encampment occupies the crumbling stone foundations of an ancient night elf settlement, long ruined even before the demons flooded the region with fel magic.",al={"what ruins are here","mannoroc ancient ruins","elf ruins desolace"}},{q="How are the demons arriving in Desolace?",a="Burning Blade cultists maintain magical summoning portals across the ruins. These portals draw continuous reinforcements directly from the Twisting Nether, frustrating outside attempts to permanently cleanse the site.",al={"where do demons come from","burning blade portals desolace"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The concentrated fel energy and active Legion summoning rifts make the coven an object of keen tactical interest, offering firsthand observation of raw demonic manifestation.",["race:NightElf"]="Seeing the stonework of your ancient ancestors desecrated and trampled by demonic invaders makes Mannoroc Coven an agonizing reminder of the War of the Ancients."},kw={"azrethoc","burning blade","coven","desolace","felhounds","infernals","jugkar grim'rod","mannoroc"},rel={"zone:desolace","topic:burning-legion","subzone:ghost-walker-post","subzone:shadowprey-village","npc:taiga-wisemane","topic:night-elf"},src={"Mannoroc Coven"}}
E["subzone:nijel-s-point"] = {t="subzone",n="Nijel's Point",z="desolace",s="Nijel's Point is a fortified Alliance and Cenarion Circle redoubt perched high on the northern bluffs of Desolace. Tucked safely away from the blighted valleys below, it serves as the sole safe haven for Alliance travelers, researchers, and soldiers navigating the harsh wasteland.",h="Nijel's Point is a fortified Alliance and Cenarion Circle redoubt perched high on the northern bluffs of...",sec={{t="A Bastion Above the Wastes",b="Carved into the sheer cliffs bordering the Stonetalon Mountains, Nijel's Point stands well above the gray dust and marauding centaur packs of Desolace. The settlement is held by a detachment of the Stormwind Army under Captain Pentigast, charged with monitoring the violent clan wars that threaten Alliance interests across southern Kalimdor. Its high elevation and narrow access trails make it readily defensible, providing a secure staging ground for couriers, scouts, and griffin riders travelling between Stonetalon Peak, Theramore, and Feathermoon Stronghold.",sp=0},{t="Cenarion and Crusade Expeditions",b="Beyond the Stormwind garrison, the outpost shelters emissaries with distinct and perilous agendas. Keeper Marandis and his dryads use the camp as an operational base to confront Princess Theradras deep within Maraudon, seeking to recover the fallen demigod Zaetar. Even the Scarlet Crusade maintains an emissary here in Brother Anton, who seeks to scour the undead ravaging the valley floor. Despite the bustling presence of soldiers and druids, the identity of Nijel himself remains an ancient mystery lost even to those garrisoned atop the ridge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Alliance stationed in Desolace?",a="Captain Pentigast leads a Stormwind Army detachment to monitor the warring centaur clans. The Alliance fears that once one clan wipes out the others, the victorious horde will turn its aggression toward neighboring territories and settlements like Stonetalon and Feralas.",al={"why is alliance here","stormwind army in desolace","why nijels point exists"}},{q="Who was Nijel?",a="Nobody at the outpost seems to know. It is widely presumed that Nijel was the founder of the ancient, ruined settlement atop the ridge, but his true history has been lost to time.",al={"who is nijel","nijel lore","who was nijels point named after"}},{q="What is the Cenarion Circle doing at Nijel's Point?",a="Keeper Marandis and his dryad sisters have come to Desolace to purge Maraudon, slay Princess Theradras, and reclaim the remains of Zaetar to return them to the sacred groves of the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"druids in nijels point","keeper marandis mission","why are dryads here"}},{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade at Nijel's Point?",a="Brother Anton serves as a distant emissary of the Scarlet Crusade, directed by Brother Crowley to recruit capable Alliance adventurers in the fight against the undead blighting Desolace.",al={"brother anton scarlet crusade","scarlet crusade in desolace"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Nijel's Point is your sole fortified refuge and flight staging ground in Desolace, linking supply lines between Stonetalon, Theramore, and Feralas.",["class:Druid"]="Keeper Marandis uses this high mountain sanctuary to organize the reclamation of Zaetar's remains from the corruption festering inside Maraudon."},kw={"brother anton","centaur","desolace","marandis","maraudon","nijel's point","outpost","pentigast"},rel={"zone:desolace","topic:stormwind-army","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:centaur","zone:stonetalon","subzone:feathermoon-stronghold","subzone:theramore-isle","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Nijel's Point"}}
E["subzone:sar-theris-strand"] = {t="subzone",n="Sar'theris Strand",z="desolace",s="Sar'theris Strand forms the western coastline of Desolace, fronting the Veiled Sea. In stark contrast to the barren, grey inland wastes, the shore is sunny and grassy, though it remains perilous due to prowling naga, sea giants, and makrura.",h="Sar'theris Strand forms the western coastline of Desolace, fronting the Veiled Sea.",sec={{t="A Green Edge on a Grey Waste",b="Running the length of western Desolace, Sar'theris Strand offers a bizarre respite from the ash and dust of the inland plains. Here, the ocean air keeps the clifftops and beaches bright and green. Yet the strand is far from welcoming: serpentine naga patrol the surf alongside towering sea giants and territorial makrura. Shipwrecks litter the shoals, including the ruined Karnitol vessel to the north and small shattered skiffs beneath the towers of Ethel Rethor, proving the sea is as treacherous as the shore.",sp=0},{t="Wreckage and Rare Waters",b="Beyond the constant threat of naga and giants, the waters off the strand are known among seasoned travelers for their peculiar bounties. The jagged coastal shallows conceal salvage from lost expeditions and merchant ventures, while the deep surf is home to rare marine wildlife, notably the prized Sar'theris Striker fish sought out by master fishermen across Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Sar'theris Strand green when the rest of Desolace is dead?",a="While the interior of Desolace was scourged into a barren wasteland by elemental devastation, the coastline catches the open air and currents of the Veiled Sea, allowing grasses and bright skies to persist along the shore.",al={"why green coast","desolace coastline grassy","sar'theris weather"}},{q="What creatures inhabit Sar'theris Strand?",a="The strand is dominated by the amphibious Slitherblade naga, wandering sea giants, and scuttling makrura. Travelers must constantly watch the surf, as patrols roam close to the water's edge.",al={"who lives here","sar'theris mobs","what monsters are on the strand"}},{q="What shipwrecks lie along the shore?",a="The Karnitol Shipwreck sits off the northern waters of the strand, while smaller vessels lie smashed on the beach bluffs beneath the ruined elven towers of Ethel Rethor.",al={"karnitol shipwreck","sunken boats strand","beach wreckage"}},{q="Why do fishermen seek out Sar'theris Strand?",a="The coastal waters here are the exclusive home of the Sar'theris Striker, an elusive fish recognized by renowned angler Nat Pagle as one of the ultimate tests of fishing mastery.",al={"sar'theris striker","fishing coast desolace","nat pagle fish"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="The strand's shores and surrounding waters offer rich marine game, including makrura and rare ocean fish, though cooking fires must be lit under the constant watch of prowling naga."},kw={"desolace","hatecrest","karnitol","makrura","sar'theris","strand","striker"},rel={"zone:desolace","subzone:ethel-rethor","topic:naga","npc:nat-pagle"},src={"Sar'theris Strand"}}
E["subzone:sargeron"] = {t="subzone",n="Sargeron",z="desolace",s="Sargeron is the crumbled ruin of an ancient night elf city located in northern Desolace. Shattered during the Great Sundering, its former temples of Elune have been defiled and claimed by the Hatefury satyrs, who renamed the grounds in tribute to their master, Sargeras.",h="Sargeron is the crumbled ruin of an ancient night elf city located in northern Desolace.",sec={{t="A Defiled Sanctuary",b="Before the War of the Ancients broke the continent, this settlement was a flourishing center of worship dedicated to Elune, housing sacred grounds such as Elune's Temple, Sanctuary, and Cathedral. Its true name is lost to antiquity. When the world shattered, the city collapsed into rubble, leaving behind sanctified relics like the Cup of Elune, Elune's Brazier, and Elune's Handmaiden. In the millennia since, corrupted Hatefury satyrs overran the stones, repurposing the sacred Kaldorei architecture into a stronghold honoring the titan Sargeras.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Sargeron called before the Sundering?",a="Its original night elven name has been lost to time. The current name, Sargeron, was given to the ruins by the Hatefury satyrs in homage to the fallen titan Sargeras.",al={"original name","sargeron original name","what was it called"}},{q="Who occupies Sargeron now?",a="The ruins are occupied by the Hatefury satyrs, corrupt demonic beings spawned during the War of the Ancients who actively desecrate the ancient elven sites.",al={"who lives here","sargeron mobs","enemies in sargeron"}},{q="What holy sites were originally located here?",a="The city held several major sites devoted to the Moon Goddess, including Elune's Temple, Elune's Sanctuary, and Elune's Cathedral, which once sheltered revered relics such as the Cup of Elune.",al={"elune temples","holy sites","what buildings were here"}},{q="Why is Sargeron significant to night elves?",a="It serves as a grim reminder of the War of the Ancients and the defilement of Kaldorei holy spaces by demonic forces, harboring ancient elven artifacts that risk being lost or corrupted.",al={"night elf lore sargeron","why do night elves care"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The ruins are a painful sight for any Kaldorei, as sacred altars of Elune are openly defiled by demonic satyrs who mock the goddess in Sargeras's name.",["class:Priest"]="Priests of the Moon will recognize remnants of Elune's Cathedral and holy relics scattered across the broken stones, urging purification."},kw={"cup of elune","desolace","elune","hatefury","kaldorei","sargeras","sargeron","satyr"},rel={"zone:desolace","topic:satyr","topic:elune","topic:sargeras","topic:night-elf","topic:war-of-the-ancients"},src={"Sargeron"}}
E["subzone:shadowbreak-ravine"] = {t="subzone",n="Shadowbreak Ravine",z="desolace",s="Shadowbreak Ravine is a secluded mountain hollow tucked away in southeastern Desolace. Cloaked among jagged crags near Shok'Thokar, this eerie ravine serves as a hidden redoubt for the demonic forces and mortal zealots of the Burning Blade.",h="Shadowbreak Ravine is a secluded mountain hollow tucked away in southeastern Desolace.",sec={{t="A Hidden Enclave of Fel",b="Tucked deep into the barren mountain ridges southeast of Shok'Thokar, Shadowbreak Ravine provides the Burning Blade with a secluded staging ground away from the eyes of wandering centaur tribes. Amid strange, oversized mushrooms and grim ritual encampments, cultists labor alongside summoned demons. Here, dark practitioners invoke fel energies and tend heavy ritual chains, using the natural isolation of the ravine to marshal reinforcements and maintain a firm demonic foothold within the badlands of Desolace.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Shadowbreak Ravine?",a="Shadowbreak Ravine is a hidden mountain ravine situated in southeastern Desolace, just beyond Shok'Thokar. It serves as a concealed camp and staging ground for demonic minions and cultists serving the Burning Blade.",al={"shadowbreak ravine info","what is this place","where is shadowbreak ravine"}},{q="Who occupies the ravine?",a="The ravine is occupied by cultists of the Burning Blade working directly alongside demons. They use the ravine's sheltered terrain to perform dark rituals and support their broader offensive across the region.",al={"who lives here","shadowbreak ravine mobs","enemies in shadowbreak ravine"}},{q="What features can be found inside the ravine?",a="The ravine contains dark ritual structures, massive iron chains, and prominent giant mushrooms that sprout amidst the fel-tainted encampments hidden within the mountain clefts.",al={"what is inside shadowbreak ravine","landmarks in shadowbreak ravine"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The dark summoning circles and concentrated fel presence make this secretive canyon a clear testament to the reach of the Burning Blade's dark arts."},kw={"burning blade","cultists","demons","desolace","fel","shadowbreak ravine","shok'thokar"},rel={"subzone:shok-thokar","zone:desolace","subzone:magram-village","topic:centaur"},src={"Shadowbreak Ravine"}}
E["subzone:shadowprey-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Shadowprey Village",z="desolace",s="Shadowprey Village is a remote Horde fishing settlement built along the rocky southern coast of Sar'theris Strand in Desolace. Populated largely by Darkspear troll fishermen and supported by tauren service keepers, it acts as a critical coastal outpost and trade lifeline amidst a barren wasteland.",h="Shadowprey Village is a remote Horde fishing settlement built along the rocky southern coast of Sar'theris...",sec={{t="A Haven on the Strand",b="Tucked against the cliffs of southern Desolace, Shadowprey Village offers safe harbor in a region notorious for centaur clans and desolate wastes. The settlement is primarily an encampment of troll fishermen whose hauls sustain not only their own village but also inland outposts like Ghost Walker Post. Despite the rough shoreline, towering wooden piers reach out into the ocean, allowing local anglers to brave deep waters and dive for shellfish among the submerged wreckage dotting Sar'theris Strand.",sp=0},{t="Coastal Tribulations",b="Maintaining a frontier port in Desolace is fraught with danger. Beyond the inland threat of marauding centaur, the ocean itself tests the village's survival. Local waters are haunted by ravenous sea life—notably the monstrous orca Blubbergut, who gorges on the fish stocks—and encroachment from violent lobstrok along the southern banks. Tauren allies, including Taiga Wisemane and the keepers of the inn and wind rider roost, help shore up defenses and keep trade routes open across Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Shadowprey Village important to the Horde?",a="Desolace is an inhospitable wasteland lacking natural resources. Shadowprey Village serves as the Horde's sole coastal port in the region, bringing in vital hauls of fish and shellfish to feed garrisons like Ghost Walker Post while offering a wind rider travel hub connected to Stonetalon, Thunder Bluff, and Feralas.",al={"shadowprey purpose","why is shadowprey here","shadowprey horde role"}},{q="Who leads Shadowprey Village?",a="The settlement does not have an official single chieftain. The village operates as a loose community of troll fishermen, with elders like Mai'Lahii handling communication with visitors such as the Cenarion Circle, while tauren residents like Taiga Wisemane oversee coastal security and local defense.",al={"shadowprey leader","who is in charge of shadowprey","mai'lahii"}},{q="Why are there tauren running the services in a troll village?",a="Shadowprey began as an indigenous Darkspear fishing outpost, but its role as a regional supply hub attracted the Horde's broader logistical apparatus. Tauren oversee essential shared infrastructure, maintaining the inn, managing the stables, and directing the wind rider roost connecting the port to Mulgore and beyond.",al={"tauren in shadowprey","why tauren here","shadowprey tauren"}},{q="What threats are troubling the fishermen?",a="Aside from hostile inland centaur, the village contends with a shortage of fish caused by a massive orca named Blubbergut devouring the coastal shoals, alongside encroaching lobstrok swarming the southern tidal flats.",al={"shadowprey problems","blubbergut","shadowprey threats"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Shadowprey is a rare haven of Darkspear coastal culture in central Kalimdor, showcasing the tribe's traditional mastery of spearfishing, diving, and coastal survival.",["faction:Horde"]="For Horde travelers trekking through Desolace, Shadowprey Village provides the only coastal rest stop, flight hub, and secure supply base south of the Kodo Graveyard."},kw={"blubbergut","desolace","mai'lahii","sar'theris strand","shadowprey","shadowprey village","taiga wisemane","troll fishing"},rel={"zone:desolace","subzone:sar-theris-strand","subzone:ghost-walker-post","npc:taiga-wisemane","topic:troll","topic:tauren","topic:horde","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Shadowprey Village"}}
E["subzone:shok-thokar"] = {t="subzone",n="Shok'Thokar",z="desolace",s="Shok'Thokar is the name given to the demon-corrupted encampment nestled against the eastern mountains of southern Desolace. Known to locals as Magram Village, the settlement sits adjacent to the blighted depths of Shadowbreak Ravine and remains a bastion for the brutal Magram centaur clan.",h="Shok'Thokar is the name given to the demon-corrupted encampment nestled against the eastern mountains of...",sec={{t="A Bastion of Bone and Dust",b="Situated in southeastern Desolace, this encampment stands in the shadow of the mountains alongside the demonic fissures of Shadowbreak Ravine. Built from rough hide tents, cracked bones, and packed earth, it serves as the heart of the savage Magram centaur clan. While outsiders and mapmakers refer to the region as Shok'Thokar, travelers across Kalimdor know it best as Magram Village. Life here is defined by relentless blood feuds against their bitter rivals, the Gelkis clan, and a grim proximity to the dark demonic influences bleeding out of the nearby ravines.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the difference between Shok'Thokar and Magram Village?",a="They are the same physical settlement. The area in southeastern Desolace where the Magram centaur make their camp is identified as Shok'Thokar on certain territorial maps, but travelers, adventurers, and locals almost universally know it as Magram Village.",al={"is this magram village","shok'thokar vs magram village","what is this place called"}},{q="Who lives in this settlement?",a="The settlement is populated by the Magram clan, one of the primary centaur tribes warring for dominance across Desolace. Their warriors, scouts, pack runners, and bonepaw hyenas guard the perimeter fiercely against intruders and rival clans.",al={"who is here","who lives here","shokthokar residents"}},{q="Why is this area significant to the centaur of Desolace?",a="The village serves as the home territory and seat of power for the Magram. From here, they wage a brutal, unending civil war against their sworn enemies, the Gelkis centaur, vying for scarce water, grazing land, and survival in the harsh wastes.",al={"why do centaur fight here","centaur clan war","magram purpose"}},{q="What is the danger of the nearby ravine?",a="Directly abutting the camp lies Shadowbreak Ravine, a rift tainted by demonic energy and the cultists of the Burning Blade. The Magram live dangerously close to this creeping corruption, exposing the area to the dark forces lurking within the wastes.",al={"why are demons near","shadowbreak connection"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Horde maintains a delicate strategy regarding the centaur in Desolace: ensuring the warring clans remain fractured and fighting each other so they can never unite into a massive army that threatens Kalimdor.",["race:Tauren"]="Centaur have brought untold suffering to the shu'halo across generations. Any centaur stronghold is viewed with wariness and vigilance by tauren travelers passing through Desolace."},kw={"centaur","desolace","gelkis","magram","magram village","shadowbreak ravine","shok'thokar"},rel={"subzone:magram-village","subzone:shadowbreak-ravine","zone:desolace","topic:centaur","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Shok'Thokar"}}
E["subzone:slitherblade-shore"] = {t="subzone",n="Slitherblade Shore",z="desolace",s="Slitherblade Shore stretches along the rugged northwestern coast of Desolace, running from the borders of Stonetalon Mountains down toward Sar'theris Strand. Dominated by hostile Slitherblade naga, the shoreline is littered with sunken shipwrecks and ancient sunken architecture that frames the promontory of Ethel Rethor.",h="Slitherblade Shore stretches along the rugged northwestern coast of Desolace, running from the borders of...",sec={{t="A Hostile Coastline",b="Slitherblade Shore encompasses the windswept tidal sands of northern Desolace, bisected by the high promontory of Ethel Rethor. Off the surf lies Ranazjar Isle, where the serpent-like Slitherblade naga hold dominion under their sea priestesses. Shipwrecks churn in the shallow waters, washed ashore against ancient night elven stonework that sank during the Great Sundering.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures inhabit Slitherblade Shore?",a="The shoreline is heavily overrun by the Slitherblade naga, who patrol the shallows, tidal banks, and sunken ruins along the coast of Desolace.",al={"who lives here","slitherblade shore enemies","mobs on shore"}},{q="Where does Slitherblade Shore begin and end?",a="The shore extends from the northern cliffs bordering the Stonetalon Mountains down south toward Sar'theris Strand, centered around the ruined promontory of Ethel Rethor.",al={"where is slitherblade shore","shore boundaries"}},{q="What are all the ruined structures in the water?",a="The stone pillars and crumbled foundations scattered along the coast and near Ranazjar Isle are the remnants of ancient night elven cities that were swallowed by the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago.",al={"why are there ruins here","sunken ruins desolace"}},{q="Why are there shipwrecks along the beach?",a="The treacherous reefs, unpredictable coastal tides, and aggressive naga presence make this stretch of sea a graveyard for vessels sailing along western Kalimdor.",al={"slitherblade shipwrecks","broken ships"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The naga infesting Slitherblade Shore are a bitter reminder of Queen Azshara's cursed legacy, defiling the drowned ruins of your ancient Highborne ancestors."},kw={"desolace","ethel rethor","naga","ranazjar isle","shipwrecks","slitherblade","slitherblade shore"},rel={"subzone:ethel-rethor","zone:desolace","subzone:sar-theris-strand","zone:stonetalon","topic:naga","topic:night-elf"},src={"Slitherblade Shore"}}
E["subzone:thunder-axe-fortress"] = {t="subzone",n="Thunder Axe Fortress",z="desolace",s="Thunder Axe Fortress is a fortified compound in northwestern Desolace serving as a stronghold for the demonic Burning Blade cult. Within its stone barracks, watchtowers, and darkened caves, cultists perform dark rituals to summon demonic entities and store stolen artifacts of power. The cult remains an active threat to anyone traversing the desolate wastes.",h="Thunder Axe Fortress is a fortified compound in northwestern Desolace serving as a stronghold for the demonic...",sec={{t="A Bastion of the Burning Blade",b="Perched in northwestern Desolace, Thunder Axe Fortress serves as a heavily guarded redoubt for the Burning Blade. Composed of stone barracks, defensive watchtowers, and deep caverns, it allows the cult to maintain a fortified foothold far from the gaze of Kalimdor's major cities. Here, the cultists gather fel energies, summon lesser demons, and concoct schemes to bring far more dangerous entities into the world.",sp=0},{t="Stolen Relics and Dark Summonings",b="The fortress has long served as a repository for stolen relics and demonic conduits. In the past, the cult stored the Hand of Iruxos here, using its power to pierce the veil and sustain demonic portals at the Mannoroc Coven. More recently, the sorcerer Tyranis Malem and his allies harbored the stolen Sceptre of Light, a powerful relic taken from the coastal naga that drew the attention of the Argent Dawn.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who controls Thunder Axe Fortress?",a="The fortress is held by the Burning Blade cult, an organization devoted to demonic power and the remnants of the Shadow Council. On the ground, the fortress and its operations are overseen by warlocks such as Tyranis Malem.",al={"who runs thunder axe fortress","who is in thunder axe fortress","thunder axe fortress boss"}},{q="What is the Sceptre of Light?",a="The Sceptre of Light is a powerful relic that the Burning Blade stole from the naga along the Desolace coast. It was held within Thunder Axe Fortress by the traitorous warlock Tyranis Malem until agents allied with the Argent Dawn intervened to recover it.",al={"sceptre of light","scepter of light","stolen naga artifact"},sp=1},{q="How is this fortress connected to Mannoroc Coven?",a="The cultists at Thunder Axe Fortress previously held an artifact known as the Hand of Iruxos. This relic was directly linked to the demon portals active at the Mannoroc Coven in southern Desolace, binding their demonic efforts across the zone.",al={"mannoroc coven connection","hand of iruxos"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The Burning Blade's experiments at the fortress demonstrate the reckless bounds of demonology, from binding lesser fiends to forcing planar rifts for greater entities.",["faction:Alliance"]="Investigating Thunder Axe Fortress aligns with Argent Dawn efforts to secure dangerous artifacts like the Sceptre of Light before fel cultists turn them against the continent."},kw={"burning blade","desolace","hand of iruxos","kohor","sceptre of light","thunder axe fortress","tyranis malem"},rel={"zone:desolace","subzone:mannoroc-coven","topic:argent-dawn","topic:naga","topic:light"},src={"Thunder Axe Fortress"}}
E["subzone:valley-of-spears"] = {t="subzone",n="Valley of Spears",z="desolace",s="The Valley of Spears is a rugged canyon nestled in western Desolace, serving as the stronghold of the Maraudine centaur clan. Enclosed by steep cliffs and guarded passes, the valley leads directly to Maraudon, the sacred ancestral burial ground of all centaurkind.",h="The Valley of Spears is a rugged canyon nestled in western Desolace, serving as the stronghold of the...",sec={{t="Stronghold of the Maraudine",b="Carved into the rugged heights of western Desolace, the Valley of Spears earned its name from the bristling defensive stakes and warlike presence of the Maraudine clan. Accessible on foot only through narrow, easily defended mountain passes from the south and east, this enclosed valley provides the centaur with a natural bastion. Travelers who venture past the rocky chokepoints face dense encampments of hostile nomads guarding the approach to their most revered holy site.",sp=0},{t="The Threshold of Maraudon",b="Tucked away at the southwestern end of the valley lies the entrance to Maraudon, the subterranean tomb complex holding the remains of the first centaur and their earth-mother, Theradras. Because of this proximity, the Maraudine defend the canyon with zealous fury against rival clans and outside interlopers alike. Anyone foolish enough to stumble into the valley unawares—such as careless gnome cartographers or scouts—frequently ends up captured or slain.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls the Valley of Spears?",a="The valley is the primary territory of the Maraudine clan, one of the warring centaur factions fighting for dominance in Desolace.",al={"who lives here","valley of spears centaur clan","maraudine base"}},{q="Where does the Valley of Spears lead?",a="At the southwestern extremity of the valley lies the entrance to Maraudon, the holy ancestral cavern and burial ground of the centaur race.",al={"how to get to maraudon","maraudon entrance","what is at the end of valley of spears"}},{q="How do you enter the valley?",a="The valley is surrounded by sheer mountain ridges and can only be entered on foot through narrow mountain defiles in the east and south.",al={"valley of spears entrance","how to get in","passes into valley of spears"}},{q="Is anyone trapped in the valley?",a="Yes, an unfortunate gnome named Melizza Brimbuzzle has been taken prisoner by the Maraudine centaur and is held within their camps.",al={"melizza brimbuzzle","captive in valley of spears","gnome prisoner"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Centaur savagery has plagued the tribes of Kalimdor for generations; navigating this stronghold brings the tauren face-to-face with the heart of that ancient enmity.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance keeps a cautious eye on the region, particularly after exploratory travelers like the gnome Melizza Brimbuzzle were captured by the hostile Maraudine clan."},kw={"centaur","desolace","maraudine","maraudon","melizza brimbuzzle","valley of spears"},rel={"zone:desolace","topic:centaur"},src={"Valley of Spears"}}
E["subzone:wicked-tunnels"] = {t="subzone",n="Wicked Tunnels",z="desolace",s="The Wicked Tunnels form the subterranean labyrinth beneath Desolace that bridges the surface caves with the depths of Maraudon. Divided into an upper maze of purple crystals and a lower path toward cascading subterranean waters, these passages are teeming with ravenous rock borers and restless earth elementals.",h="The Wicked Tunnels form the subterranean labyrinth beneath Desolace that bridges the surface caves with the...",sec={{t="The Threshold of Maraudon",b="Carved deep beneath the arid wastes of Desolace, the Wicked Tunnels branch outward from the cavern known as Zaetar's Choice. Venturing into the northern route leads travelers into the upper tunnels, a disorienting, multi-tiered maze of natural stone bridges illuminated by strange purple crystals. Here, tunneling rock borers and protective earth elementals prowl, guarding the path toward Maraudon's Wicked Grotto. Following the eastern passage through Earth Song Gate reveals the lower tunnels: a direct, quieter descent leading straight toward the roar of Earth Song Falls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do the Wicked Tunnels lead?",a="The tunnels serve as the outer entryways into the sacred centaur tomb-city of Maraudon. The upper maze winds toward the Wicked Grotto portal, while the lower branch guides travelers directly to the falls of Earth Song.",al={"wicked tunnels destination","where do these tunnels go","wicked tunnels entrance"}},{q="What creatures dwell within the tunnels?",a="The cavern walls are crawled by subterranean rock borers and guarded by wandering earth elementals bound to the troubled earth of Desolace.",al={"wicked tunnels mobs","what lives in wicked tunnels"}},{q="How do you reach the lower Wicked Tunnels?",a="From the junction at Zaetar's Choice, take the eastern path through the Earth Song Gate. It presents a much shorter, more direct tunnel compared to the winding upper maze.",al={"reach lower tunnels","how to get to lower wicked tunnels"}},{q="Why are the upper tunnels glowing purple?",a="The upper caverns are encrusted with clusters of luminescent purple subterranean crystals, casting an eerie glow over the bridges and chasms that lead toward the Wicked Grotto.",al={"purple crystals wicked tunnels","why is it purple in wicked tunnels"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The chaotic agitation among the resident earth elementals mirrors the deep spiritual wound echoing across the subterranean foundation of Desolace.",["profession:Mining"]="The twisting stone caverns and elemental denizens mark these passages as a prime territory for precious subterranean mineral deposits."},kw={"desolace","earth elementals","earth song falls","maraudon","rock borers","wicked grotto","wicked tunnels","zaetar's choice"},rel={"subzone:zaetar-s-choice","zone:desolace"},src={"Wicked Tunnels"}}
E["subzone:zaetar-s-choice"] = {t="subzone",n="Zaetar's Choice",z="desolace",s="Zaetar's Choice is a cavernous crossroads deep within the approach to Maraudon in western Desolace. Named for the demigod Zaetar, progenitor of the centaur race, this junction splits into three paths leading to distinct wings of the sacred underground complex.",h="Zaetar's Choice is a cavernous crossroads deep within the approach to Maraudon in western Desolace.",sec={{t="The Fork in the Earth",b="Descending through the outer caves of Maraudon brings explorers to Zaetar's Choice, the primary subterranean crossroads before entering the sanctum proper. Marked by contrasting crystal formations and ominous stone carvings, the cavern forks into three distinct routes. The left passageway glows with purple crystal and winds into the Wicked Tunnels toward the Wicked Grotto. To the right, bathed in orange crystal light, lies the route through the Foulspore Pools into Foulspore Cavern. Flanked by massive statues, the central route breaches the Earth Song Gate directly toward the lower falls.",sp=0},{t="A Legacy of Ruin",b="The chamber draws its name from Zaetar, son of the demigod Cenarius. Drawn into an unnatural union with Princess Theradras, an elemental power trapped beneath the earth, Zaetar fathered the first centaur. Horrified by the barbaric savagery of their own offspring, Zaetar was slain by his children, leaving Maraudon as both his tomb and the centaur's holiest shrine. Standing at this fork, adventurers stand at the threshold where Kalimdor's balance was torn asunder.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does each path lead from Zaetar's Choice?",a="The left tunnel, illuminated by purple crystals, routes through the upper Wicked Tunnels to the Wicked Grotto. The right tunnel, gleaming with orange crystals, heads into the Foulspore Pools and Foulspore Cavern. The central gate, flanked by statues, bypasses these outer wings directly toward the Earth Song Falls.",al={"which way to go in maraudon","maraudon portal directions","purple or orange side"}},{q="Who was Zaetar?",a="Zaetar was a keeper of the grove and son of Cenarius. He fell in love with Princess Theradras, the elemental daughter of Therazane. Their union birthed the first centaur, who promptly turned violent and slew Zaetar, entombing his remains deep within Maraudon.",al={"who is zaetar","zaetar lore","zaetar father of centaur"}},{q="Why is this area called a choice?",a="The name reflects both the literal split in the caverns, where spelunkers must decide whether to delve into the purple Wicked Grotto, the orange Foulspore Cavern, or the central gate, and the tragic historical choice Zaetar made in communing with the earth elemental Theradras.",al={"why is it called zaetars choice","zaetar choice meaning"}},{q="Is Zaetar's Choice safe from enemies?",a="While it functions as a staging point for adventurers preparing to enter the inner portals of Maraudon, the outer caverns around it are still prowled by troggs, subterranean oozes, and occasional rare beasts.",al={"are there monsters at zaetars choice","zaetars choice safe"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids, traversing Zaetar's Choice carries a solemn weight; it marks the tragic descent of one of Cenarius's favored sons into ruin, an unnatural liaison that forever blighted the lands of Kalimdor.",["race:Tauren"]="Centuries of brutal warfare against the centaur make any site honoring Zaetar deeply resonant for the tauren, whose ancestral struggle originated directly from the sins committed in these caverns."},kw={"centaur","desolace","earth song gate","foulspore pools","maraudon","wicked tunnels","zaetar","zaetar's choice"},rel={"zone:desolace","topic:centaur","subzone:wicked-tunnels","subzone:foulspore-pools","subzone:crossroads"},src={"Zaetar's Choice"}}
E["zone:desolace"] = {t="zone",n="Desolace",z="desolace",s="Desolace is a bleak, windswept desert on Kalimdor's western coast, defined by cracked gray earth, constant stormy skies, and the bones of fallen beasts. It is the ancestral cradle of the vicious centaur race and a contested wasteland scarred by ancient Highborne ruins, encroaching demonic cults, and bitter tribal warfare. Both the Horde and Alliance maintain precarious footholds amidst the dust, each seeking to carve out influence while warding off spreading corruption.",h="Desolace is a bleak, windswept desert on Kalimdor's western coast, defined by cracked gray earth, constant...",sec={{t="A Land Cursed and Broken",b="Desolace was not always a barren expanse of ash and yellowed pools. Over a millennium ago, it was Mashan'she—a lush meadowland tended by tauren shaman. That paradise unraveled when the earth elemental Princess Theradras awakened from beneath the soil, draining the surrounding life force to regenerate her form. The calamity summoned Zaetar, son of Cenarius, but rather than subduing her, he took the princess as his mate. From their unnatural union sprang the first centaur. In shame and bloodthirsty wrath, the newborn race murdered their father, overran the verdant plains, and drove the tauren away, leaving behind the scarred wasteland known today.",sp=0},{t="Warring Hooves",b="The interior of Desolace echoes with the thunder of thousands of hooves as four splintered centaur tribes wage endless war against all interlopers and each other. The Kolkar roam the eastern cliffs, the Magram hold crude yurts around brackish sinkholes, the Gelkis dwell behind rope bridges in deep southern ravines, and the fanatical Maraudine defend the approach to Maraudon itself. Travelers venturing across the wastes frequently find themselves drawn into this ancient blood feud, forced to slaughter one tribe to gain safe passage and tenuous parley with another.",sp=0},{t="Cults and Shadowed Coasts",b="Beyond the warring centaur, darker perils fester along the borders. The Burning Blade cult operates freely out of Thunder Axe Fortress and Shadowbreak Ravine, summoning demons and satyrs that threaten to drown the region in fel fire. Along the stormy shoreline, naga creep onto the beaches of Ethel Rethor, while Darkspear trolls spear fish from the stilted platforms of Shadowprey Village. Tucked high in the northern crags, the Alliance watches from Nijel's Point, suspicious of the Horde's expansion and ever wary of the demonic taint spreading from Mannoroc Coven.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Desolace such a dead wasteland?",a="Centuries ago, the land was a fertile meadow called Mashan'she. Tauren shaman accidentally roused the slumbering earth elemental Princess Theradras, who consumed the vitality of the region to rebuild her physical form. The birth and violent expansion of the centaur shortly after destroyed whatever plant life survived, leaving only gray dust and ash.",al={"why is desolace dead","what happened to mashan'she","desolace lore origin"}},{q="Where did the centaur come from?",a="The centaur are the offspring of Zaetar, son of the demigod Cenarius, and the elemental Princess Theradras. Disgusted and enraged by their own twisted appearance, the first khans slew their father immediately after birth and multiplied across the plains in a frenzy of brutality.",al={"centaur origin","who made the centaur","zaetar theradras"}},{q="Can I ally with the centaur tribes here?",a="Yes. Adventurers can earn reputation with either the Gelkis or the Magram tribe by slaying members of their rival clan. Gaining enough standing with one unlocks access to their village, tribal quests, and peace within their territory, though it makes the opposing tribe permanently hostile.",al={"centaur reputation","gelkis or magram","how to befriend centaur"}},{q="What is Maraudon?",a="Maraudon is the sacred ancestral burial ground of the centaur race, hidden deep within the twisting western cliffs of Desolace. It serves as both the tomb of Zaetar and the subterranean lair of Princess Theradras, who continues to channel dark elemental corruption through its cavernous halls.",al={"where is maraudon","maraudon dungeon","what lies under desolace"}},{q="Who is the wanderer roaming Desolace with a bear?",a="That is Rexxar, the Champion of the Horde, accompanied by his loyal bear companion Misha. The Mok'Nathal wanderer patrols the dusty highways of Desolace and the Stonetalon Mountains, keeping a watchful eye on the wilderness and assisting those on vital Horde business.",al={"rexxar desolace","beastmaster in desolace","who is the orc with a bear"}},{q="Why are the Alliance and Horde fighting the Burning Blade here?",a="The Burning Blade cult has taken over strongholds like Thunder Axe Fortress to summon demons and bind felsteeds. The demons and satyrs it calls up threaten a region-wide demonic infestation, a danger both the Horde and the Alliance must answer.",al={"burning blade desolace","thunder axe fortress cultists","why are demons here"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For the tauren, Desolace is sacred and tragic ground. Once known as Mashan'she, it was the nomadic home of your ancestors before the awakening of Theradras and the scourge of the centaur drove your people onto the brink of extinction.",["class:Warlock"]="The arid plains and demonic sites like Mannoroc Coven draw dark practitioners seeking the secrets of felsteeds, majestic wild horses twisted into fire-breathing horrors through forbidden Shadow Council rites.",["class:Druid"]="Cenarion Circle druids view Desolace as a horrifying scar upon the natural order, where Zaetar met his tragic demise and elemental decay chokes the earth.",["faction:Alliance"]="Operating out of Nijel's Point, the Alliance monitors both the treacherous centaur tribes and the suspicious spread of Horde settlements like Shadowprey Village alongside demonic cults.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde strives to secure the coastline at Shadowprey Village and protect the kodo herds at Ghost Walker Post, while fighting relentlessly to crush the Burning Blade and prove the modern Horde is free of demonic influence."},kw={"burning blade","centaur","desolace","gelkis","magram","maraudon","nijel's point","shadowprey village","theradras","zaetar"},rel={"subzone:nijel-s-point","subzone:shadowprey-village","subzone:kodo-graveyard","subzone:gelkis-village","subzone:magram-village","subzone:thunder-axe-fortress","subzone:mannoroc-coven","zone:stonetalon"},src={"Desolace (Classic)","Desolace"}}
